# PostgreSQL connection string.
#
# Used at BUILD TIME for the storefront (getStaticPaths/page frontmatter,
# migrate/seed scripts) and, as of Phase 1 (Admin Foundation), also AT
# REQUEST TIME by the on-demand /admin/*, /api/admin/*, and
# /api/auth/[...all] routes (see astro.config.mjs's adapter and each of
# those routes' `export const prerender = false`). The storefront itself
# (/, /products/*, /vi/*, /zh/*, etc.) is still fully prerendered static
# HTML and does not read this at request time.
#
# Local dev / this cloud sandbox: any plain PostgreSQL connection string.
#
# On Vercel (Neon): use Neon's POOLED connection string specifically —
# the one whose hostname contains "-pooler" (toggle "Pooled connection"
# on in the Neon dashboard's connection-string panel). See the driver
# research notes in src/server/db/client.ts for why: it's fully
# compatible with the existing `pg` driver (no code change needed) and is
# Neon's own recommended string for "many short-lived connections"
# workloads like serverless functions. Do NOT use the direct (non-pooled)
# string for the app's runtime DATABASE_URL — that one is for
# long-lived/administrative connections (e.g. running drizzle-kit migrate
# from your own machine is fine with either).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in a real connection string before
# running `npm run db:migrate`, `npm run db:seed`, `npm run seed:admin`,
# `npm run dev`, or `npm run build`.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/medicinal_herbs"

# Better Auth — required by src/server/auth/auth.ts. Generate a real
# secret with `openssl rand -base64 32`; never commit the real value.
# Use a DIFFERENT secret for the Vercel deployment than any value used
# locally — regenerate, don't reuse.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="replace-with-a-real-random-secret"

# This deployment's own canonical origin (no trailing slash, no path).
# Better Auth uses it as its baseURL — which also determines the
# automatically-trusted Origin (see the comment on `baseURL` in
# src/server/auth/auth.ts) — and src/server/auth/csrf.ts uses it as the
# only trusted Origin for mutating /api/admin/* requests. It also governs
# whether Better Auth marks its session cookie `Secure` (HTTPS origins
# only get a Secure cookie).
#
# Local dev / this cloud sandbox:
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:4321"
#
# On Vercel: this MUST be the real production HTTPS domain Vercel assigns
# the project (e.g. "https://your-project.vercel.app", or a custom domain
# if one is attached) — never localhost, and never a Vercel *preview*
# deployment's per-deploy URL, since that changes on every preview build.
# Getting this wrong breaks sign-in in two ways at once: the session
# cookie won't be marked Secure correctly for the actual origin, and
# src/server/auth/csrf.ts's Origin check on /api/admin/* will reject
# every real request because its "trusted origin" won't match what the
# browser is actually sending.
